<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Reading path</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: The Bronze Age Collapse</h1><p class="ws-lede">How a connected world of great kings fell apart around 1200 BCE, and what grew in its place.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/paths/bronze-age-collapse">Open the path &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the stops in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the stops from 1 (earliest) to 4 (latest), by when each began: a state&#8217;s founding, a person&#8217;s birth, the date of an event.</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Hittite Empire</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Battle of Kadesh</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Late Bronze Age collapse</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Kingdom of Ugarit</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Key terms</h2><p class="ws-how">The path uses these words. Explain each one in your own words.</p><ul class="ws-terms"><li><b>Akkadian language</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><b>Chariot</b><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>Stop 1, <b>Late Bronze Age</b>. The path begins here because: &#8220;An age of great territorial powers, Egypt, the Hittites, Mitanni, Babylon and Assyria, linked by diplomacy, trade and chariot warfare.&#8221; What does this stop tell you about how the story began?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Stop 5, <b>Kingdom of Ugarit</b>: &#8220;A rich port whose last letters report enemy ships off the coast; it was sacked and burned around 1185 BCE and never rebuilt.&#8221; Find one detail on its page that supports this, and one question it leaves open.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Stop 9, <b>Iron Age</b>: &#8220;Iron replaced bronze for tools and weapons from around 1200 BCE, in an age of new kingdoms, hillforts and first written records.&#8221; How does this last stop connect to an earlier one?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>The path sums itself up as: &#8220;How a connected world of great kings fell apart around 1200 BCE, and what grew in its place.&#8221; Which stop shows this best? Explain your choice.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/paths/bronze-age-collapse. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: The Bronze Age Collapse</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the stops in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Kingdom of Ugarit <span>from 1800 BCE</span></li><li>Hittite Empire <span>from 1650 BCE</span></li><li>Battle of Kadesh <span>1274 BCE</span></li><li>Late Bronze Age collapse <span>c. 1200 BCE</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Key terms</h2><dl class="ws-key-terms"><dt>Akkadian language</dt><dd>Akkadian is an extinct Semitic language of ancient Mesopotamia, written in cuneiform.</dd><dt>Chariot</dt><dd>A chariot is a light, two-wheeled, horse-drawn vehicle used in warfare, carrying a driver and an archer or spearman.</dd></dl></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers use details from the pages of the path.</p></section></div></details>
